</description></repo><application id="io.subfrost.frtun"><id>io.subfrost.frtun</id><added>2026-02-15</added><lastupdated>2026-02-15</lastupdated><name>frtun</name><summary>Privacy-first overlay network with onion routing</summary><desc>frtun is a privacy-first overlay network client with onion routing,
post-quantum cryptography, and censorship resistance.

Features:
* 3-hop onion circuit routing for anonymous connectivity
* Post-quantum key exchange (ML-KEM/Kyber) and signatures (ML-DSA/Dilithium)
* Traffic obfuscation to bypass deep packet inspection
* DNS interception with .peer name resolution
* Gateway mode for full internet routing through exit peers
* Site-to-site VPN with subnet routing and DNS zones
* Rendezvous hidden services for hosting behind NAT
* Firewall rules with per-flow forwarding, blocking, and circuit routing
* Gossip-based peer mesh for decentralized relay discovery
* Per-app VPN bypass or allow-only mode
* Quick Settings tile for one-tap connect/disconnect

All traffic is encrypted with ChaCha20-Poly1305 over Noise protocol
framework sessions with quantum-resistant key encapsulation.
